comments.content:
Workspace-link allow-list re-opens the original `.app`/`.command` RCE vector. `l.kind != "url"` accepts `file`/`folder`/`app`/`command` (and any future kind), so any workspace-link row whose `kind` is `app`/`command` is forwarded to `opener.open_path`, which on macOS launches `.app` bundles and on Linux executes `.desktop` files. If workspace-link rows can be planted (LLM output, sync partner, prior DB compromise), the very RCE that the doc comment at `open_file_path` warns about is reachable through a different channel. Tighten the allow-list to a small explicit set of kinds (e.g. only `file`/`folder`) and add an extension/launchability check (`.app`/`.command`/`.desktop` rejected).

```rust
