Scoring weights are not renormalized when only the *item* is missing an embedding. The header doc explicitly says "无向量（降级模式 / 条目缺 embedding）时…剩余权重归一（÷0.45）" — both the degraded-query case and the missing-embedding case — but the branch condition only checks `query_emb.is_some()`. When `query_emb.is_some() && item.embedding.is_none()`, `semantic` is 0 (cosine returns None → `unwrap_or(0.0)`), the 0.55 weight is silently dropped, and the item's score is computed with the unnormalized form `0.55*0 + 0.20*kw + 0.15*imp + 0.10*rec`, capping the score at ~0.45 instead of ~1.0. Such items can never beat embedding-bearing items with even moderate semantic scores, contradicting the documented intent. Fix by gating the renormalization on `query_emb.is_some() && item.embedding.is_some()` (and similarly hardening the `kw == 0.0` guard to also include `item.embedding.is_none()` if you want symmetric handling).

```rust
if query_emb.is_some() && item.embedding.is_some() {
    0.55 * semantic + 0.20 * kw + 0.15 * imp + 0.10 * rec
} else {
    // 任一向量缺失：语义项为 0，剩余权重归一（0.20+0.15+0.10=0.45）
    (0.20 * kw + 0.15 * imp + 0.10 * rec) / 0.45
}
```

