The pinned-exclusion filter is O(n*m): for every non-pinned item it linearly scans the entire pinned set via `pinned.iter().any(|p| p.id == m.id)`. As the memory store grows this turns scoring into quadratic time on every query. Build a `HashSet<&str>` (or `HashSet<String>`) of pinned ids once before the iteration and test membership in O(1):

```rust
let pinned_ids: HashSet<&str> = pinned.iter().map(|p| p.id.as_str()).collect();
let mut scored: Vec<(f64, MemItem)> = if query_kws.is_empty() && query_emb.is_none() {
    Vec::new()
} else {
    items
        .iter()
        .filter(|m| !pinned_ids.contains(m.id.as_str()))
        .map(|m| (hybrid_score(&query_kws, query_emb, m, now_ms), m.clone()))
        .filter(|(s, _)| *s > 0.0)
        .collect()
};
```

