Every `MemItem` is cloned multiple times through the pipeline: once into `pinned` (line 132), once into `scored` (line 141), and lessons get cloned again on line 150. Since `MemItem` carries non-trivial payloads (`Vec<String>` tags, `String` content, `Vec<f32>` embedding), these redundant copies multiply the allocation cost on every query. Either partition `scored` in place by `kind` (no extra clone, lessons and hits come from the same sorted Vec), or store items behind an `Arc<MemItem>` / work with indices into `items` and clone only at the very end. The same applies to `hybrid_search` (line 195) which clones every item even though the caller only needs the top-n — clone inside `.take(top_n)`, not before `.filter`.

```rust
// partition first, then take — no double clone
let (lessons, rest): (Vec<_>, Vec<_>) =
    scored.into_iter().partition(|(_, m)| m.kind == "lesson");
let lessons: Vec<MemItem> = lessons
    .into_iter()
    .take(MEMORY_LESSON_N)
    .map(|(_, m)| m)
    .collect();
let hits: Vec<MemItem> = rest
    .into_iter()
    .take(MEMORY_TOP_N)
    .map(|(_, m)| m)
    .collect();
```

