`m.kind` is a raw `String` (or `&str`) compared against string literals (`"profile"`, `"preference"`, `"lesson"`, `"summary"`, `"reflection"`) at multiple call sites. A typo such as `"leson"` or `"prefernce"` from a writer is silently accepted by these comparisons, dropping the item into the wrong bucket or into none at all — and the failure only surfaces as "memory injection returns nothing useful" at runtime. Model the kind as an enum (or a validated newtype) and centralize the parsing at the storage boundary so invalid values are unrepresentable downstream:

