`parse_http_version` accepts `HTTP/2.0` and `HTTP/3.0`, but `next()` then unconditionally rejects anything > HTTP/1.1 with a 505. The parser is therefore inconsistent with the runtime policy and `Request` objects can briefly carry unsupported versions before being discarded. Either reject unknown/unsupported versions in `parse_http_version` directly (so the parser is the single source of truth), or drop those arms from the match.

