Substring matching on the `Connection` header is not token-aware. `val.contains("close")` matches `"close-foo"` or even `"closer"`, and similarly for `"upgrade"` and `"keep-alive"`. Per RFC 7230 the value is a comma-separated list of tokens, so non-token substring matches can cause the server to incorrectly close a keep-alive connection (or vice versa). Split on commas and trim each token before comparing.

