Fallback constructs a plain object `{ code, message, recoverable }` and passes it to `handleCommandError`, while the two earlier branches forward the real `Error` instance caught from the Promise. If `handleCommandError` expects an `Error` (e.g. reads `.stack`, `instanceof Error`, calls `error.message` without null check, or coerces with `String(error)` expecting the default `Error.prototype.toString`), the fallback path will silently misbehave and the user will see no useful message — defeating the header's stated "失败可见" design goal. Make the synthetic error an actual `Error` (or a documented contract object that the helper knows how to consume).

```ts
const err = new Error(`无法识别的链接目标：${target}`);
(err as any).code = "INVALID_ARGUMENT";
(err as any).recoverable = false;
handleCommandError(err, "open link");
```

