**Stale closure over `sub.text` in the commit callback.** The `onCommit` passed to `useInlineEdit` closes over `sub.text`, so if the parent re-renders with a new `sub.text` (e.g. remote sync, undo, or another row's edit affecting shared state) while this row is in edit mode, the `text !== sub.text` comparison runs against the original value. Result: either a legitimate save is dropped (`text === stale sub.text` even though it differs from the fresh value) or a no-op save is forwarded. Add `sub.text` (and `onCommit`) to a ref inside the callback, or read fresh text via a ref that tracks `sub.text` on every render.

```ts
const subTextRef = useRef(sub.text);
subTextRef.current = sub.text;
// ...
onCommit: (d) => {
  const text = d.trim();
  if (text && text !== subTextRef.current) onCommit(text);
  setEditing(false);
},
```

