comments.content:
**`readOnly` is not enforced when entering edit mode, and never resets in-flight `editing` state.** (1) The text span's `onClick` correctly bails out when `readOnly`, but flipping `readOnly` from false → true while the input is already mounted leaves the `<input>` rendered with no `readOnly`/`disabled` attribute and no guard, so the user can keep typing and even fire `onCommit`, contradicting the read-only contract. (2) There is no effect that calls `setEditing(false)` when `readOnly` changes to `true` (or when `sub.id` changes). Add an effect that resets `editing` when `readOnly || !sub.id` becomes true, and apply `readOnly`/`disabled` to the input.

```ts
useEffect(() => {
  if (readOnly) setEditing(false);
}, [readOnly]);
```

